description:
Shipped-web 09133d9 bumped to Papyrus 5.33.0 with `proposals: { publish: true }`. Amplify job 69 then failed at the CDK assembly: FunctionDirectiveStack had 505 resources against a maximum of 500, an engine problem. 5c43894 reverted to 5.31.0 so main stays deployable.

Next: when the Papyrus patch (5.33.1 or later) is on both npm and PyPI:
- re-apply the bump from branch chore/papyrus-5.33.0, updating the version numbers to the patch;
- keep `proposals: { publish: true }` and its test;
- deploy, then check /proposals/ and /_data/proposals/index.json.

Acceptance: the deploy succeeds, proposals stay public, and the newsroom shows the Notification Center.
